.policy "ruff-pyi043-t-suffixed-type-alias" revision 2
.description "Don't end a private type alias name with a T suffix; that suffix is the convention for type variables, so it misleads readers."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff PYI043 (flake8-pyi), every file: a private type alias (`_x: TypeAlias = …` or `type _x = …`) whose name
// ends in a lowercase letter and `T`, optionally with one digit. A `T` suffix marks a type variable.
//   _FooT: TypeAlias = int        ← PYI043
//   _T: TypeAlias = int           fine: no letter before the T
#include "python/typing.rr"

.violation PYI043(at: node, x: symbol) code "PYI043" "Rename private type alias `{x}` so it no longer ends in `T` (or `T` plus a digit), e.g. by dropping the `T`, and update its references; that suffix conventionally marks a type variable."
    suppress ruff "PYI043"
PYI043(n, x) :- alias_name(n, x), match("_.*[a-z]T[0-9]?", x).
